{"id": "tea:pranagnihotra-upanisad:1", "source": "src:pranagnihotra-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "This teaching frees from saṃsāra even without agnihotra, Sāṃkhya or yoga: the body itself is the sacrifice.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:inner-sacrifice"], "practices": ["prc:pranagnihotra"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pranagnihotra-upanisad:1-4", "source": "src:pranagnihotra-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1-4"}, "paraphrase": "The sacrifice in the body: food is purified with mantras and offered into the breaths as into the sacrificial fires; the body's fires are named, and the self, intellect, mind and senses are identified with the sacrificer, his wife and the priests; the one who performs this bodily sacrifice is freed from saṃsāra.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:pranagnihotra", "cpt:internalized-sacrifice"], "practices": ["prc:pranagnihotra"], "notes": "Whole-text summary; section numbering and the exact list of correspondences not verified (low).", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U02-brahmana-vedanga"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:pranagnihotra-upanisad:2-4", "source": "src:pranagnihotra-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2-4"}, "paraphrase": "Before eating one sprinkles the food with mantras and offers five oblations to prāṇa, apāna, vyāna, udāna and samāna; the parts of the body are the fire, the priests and the ritual implements.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:pranagnihotra"], "concepts": ["cpt:ten-vayus"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
